rsx metal backend: the record cap (ENG_MAX_RECORDS) may be defined at build time.

The Metal backend records at most 8192 draws, clears and copies per submission and drops the rest of the frame. A
Resistance 3 firefight records ~7800 draws a frame besides its clears and copies; the log showed "[rsx engine/metal]
dropped 117-195 record(s) (cap 8192)" every few frames throughout the Haven fight, i.e. geometry missing from those
frames. The default stays 8192; the port defines 16384 from its own build, like RSX_DRAW_ENGINE_TEXTURE_CACHE.

With 16384 the "dropped" line is gone from the same scripted Haven run (0 lines in 280 s, against several a minute).

The macOS workflow builds libs/video/tests/test_metal_vertex_cache.m a second time with -DENG_MAX_RECORDS=16384 and
-DRSX_TEST_EXPECT_MAX_RECORDS=16384: the test asserts the cap it was built with, and its cap check finds the boundary
at 16384. Without the change that build fails the assertion (8192 == 16384).

Upstream: not proposed yet.
---

diff --git a/.github/workflows/macos.yml b/.github/workflows/macos.yml
index ad3d1512..d7f2289c 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/macos.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/macos.yml
@@ -179,2 +179,9 @@ jobs:
           /tmp/test_metal_vertex_cache
+          # Again with the record cap a title defines at build time: the cap
+          # test then finds the boundary at 16384.
+          clang -fobjc-arc -DENG_MAX_RECORDS=16384 -DRSX_TEST_EXPECT_MAX_RECORDS=16384 \
+            -I include -I libs/video libs/video/tests/test_metal_vertex_cache.m \
+            -Wl,-dead_strip -framework Metal -framework Cocoa -framework QuartzCore \
+            -o /tmp/test_metal_vertex_cache_16k
+          /tmp/test_metal_vertex_cache_16k
 
diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m b/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
index a2159290..c757541e 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
@@ -2542,3 +2542,9 @@ static void release_surfaces(void)
 #define ENG_MAX_PIPES    4096
+/* Draws, clears and copies recorded per submission; past it the rest of the
+ * frame is dropped ("dropped N record(s)"). A title with more defines a
+ * larger cap at build time: a Resistance 3 firefight records ~7800 draws
+ * besides its clears and copies. */
+#ifndef ENG_MAX_RECORDS
 #define ENG_MAX_RECORDS  8192
+#endif
 #define ENG_MAX_VIEWS    256
diff --git a/libs/video/tests/test_metal_vertex_cache.m b/libs/video/tests/test_metal_vertex_cache.m
index 9b239f96..023bc6be 100644
--- a/libs/video/tests/test_metal_vertex_cache.m
+++ b/libs/video/tests/test_metal_vertex_cache.m
@@ -17,2 +17,9 @@
 
+/* A title whose frames record more defines a larger record cap at build
+ * time; the workflow builds this test a second time with one. */
+#ifdef RSX_TEST_EXPECT_MAX_RECORDS
+_Static_assert(ENG_MAX_RECORDS == RSX_TEST_EXPECT_MAX_RECORDS,
+               "the record cap given at build time is the one the backend uses");
+#endif
+
 static int g_failures;
